@* Ported from Widgets/LinksWidget.ascx + .ascx.cs + .ascx.designer.cs - the dashboard widget
   that links out to the MixERP documentation, source, issues, forum and Facebook page.

   The whole widget was built procedurally (CreateWidget / CreateHeader / CreateList /
   AddListItem with HtmlGenericControl + HtmlControlHelper) into
   <asp:PlaceHolder ID="Placeholder1">. It is markup now, in the IDENTICAL child order and with
   the identical ids and css classes the control tree rendered:

     div#LinksWidget.four.wide.column.widget
       > div.ui.attached.segment                 (HtmlControlHelper.GetSegment("ui attached segment"))
           > div.ui.left.floated.column > div.ui.header    (the title)
           > div.ui.right.floated.column > the four icons, in order:
                 expand disabled icon, move icon, help icon, close icon
       > div.ui.attached.segment > ul > five <li> > <a target="_blank">

   The id and the "widget" class matter: the host's dashboard script finds, drags and closes a
   widget by them, and the four icons are its expand/move/help/close affordances.

   The five links are reproduced with their URLs, their localized texts and THEIR ORDER
   unchanged (documentation, source code, bugs, support, Facebook), each with target="_blank" as
   HtmlAnchor.Target set it.

   ⚠ A WIDGET DOES NOT INHERIT CurrentLogin. MixERPWidget derives from MixERPUserControlBase,
   not from MixERPUserControl, so the [Inject] ICurrentLogin / IMixERPAuthorization properties
   are absent. This widget needs neither - it has no login-derived value and runs no query - so
   nothing is injected, and that is deliberate rather than an omission.

   The original declared no OverridePath, MasterPageId, RemoveTheme, IsLandingPage or
   AccessLevel override (so it keeps MixERPWidgetBase's AccessLevel.PolicyBased) and implemented
   no ITransaction. *@

@inherits MixERP.Net.Framework.Controls.MixERPWidget
@using MixERP.Net.Common.Helpers
@using MixERP.Net.i18n.Resources

<div id="LinksWidget" class="four wide column widget">
    <div class="ui attached segment">
        <div class="ui left floated column">
            <div class="ui header">@Titles.MixERPLinks</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ui right floated column">
            @((MarkupString)HtmlControlHelper.GetIcon("expand disabled icon"))
            @((MarkupString)HtmlControlHelper.GetIcon("move icon"))
            @((MarkupString)HtmlControlHelper.GetIcon("help icon"))
            @((MarkupString)HtmlControlHelper.GetIcon("close icon"))
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ui attached segment">
        <ul>
            <li><a href="http://docs.mixerp.org" target="_blank">@Titles.Documentation</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/mixerp/mixerp" target="_blank">@Titles.DownloadSourceCode</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/mixerp/mixerp/issues" target="_blank">@Titles.SubmitBugs</a></li>
            <li><a href="http://mixerp.org/forum/" target="_blank">@Titles.Support</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.facebook.com/mixerp.official" target="_blank">@Titles.MixERPOnFacebook</a></li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    ///     MixERPUserControlBase.OnControlLoad is abstract, so every ported control declares it.
    ///     The legacy body ONLY called CreateWidget(), which built the static markup above - it
    ///     ran no query and read no login value - so there is nothing procedural left to run.
    /// </summary>
    public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
    }
}
